  annotation "note_1771578286040_2", anchor: "targets sometimes survive, left with years of pressure-memory that never resolves", text: "The cruelest line in the entry, and I wrote it as an aside about quality control. The Exchange's incompetence produces a worse outcome than the Wake-Singers' expertise. Orca ritualists at least finish what they start. A merchant guild that half-weaponizes deep-memory and leaves the remainder lodged in a living mind — that is not a failed weapon. That is a new one.", type: :commentary, display: :full
